# /etc/default/heimdall — environment for heimdall.service.
#
# Installed 0640 root:heimdall. Unlike /etc/heimdall/heimdall.toml this file is
# read by systemd, not parsed by heimdall, so it is the right place for secrets:
# dpkg does not diff it against a shipped version on upgrade.

# Extra arguments appended to:
#   /usr/bin/heimdall run-spo --config /etc/heimdall/heimdall.toml $HEIMDALL_ARGS
#
# Empty is the right default, and there is deliberately nothing to put here for a
# normal node. `run-spo` takes no cadence flag and no dry-run flag:
#
#   * there is no --interval-secs. Movements fall on the protocol's on-chain batch
#     grid (B_i = epoch_start + i x tm_batch_interval), which every SPO reads from
#     the bridge Config, so there is no local cadence to set. This file used to
#     carry `--interval-secs 900` — a `run-mover` flag — and `run-spo` rejects
#     unknown arguments, so the unit died on startup before reaching any check.
#
#   * there is no --broadcast. That is a `run-mover` flag too. A configured,
#     registered node participates from its first start; the way to watch an
#     install before enabling it is the dry run below, which joins nothing.
#
#       sudo -u heimdall heimdall run-spo --config /etc/heimdall/heimdall.toml --check
#
# What DOES belong here, if anything: --log-level / --log-format. Prefer $RUST_LOG
# at the bottom of this file for verbosity — it is finer-grained and needs no
# restart argument.
HEIMDALL_ARGS=""

# Cardano wallet mnemonic. Precedence is: cardano.mnemonic in heimdall.toml >
# $HEIMDALL_MNEMONIC — so setting it here only takes effect while cardano.mnemonic
# stays commented out in /etc/heimdall/heimdall.toml. That is the intended
# arrangement: the seed lives here, not in the file dpkg tracks.
#HEIMDALL_MNEMONIC="word word word ..."

# Log verbosity, overriding [log].level in /etc/heimdall/heimdall.toml. This is
# the better place to turn detail up on a running node: it is not a conffile, so
# dpkg will not diff it against a shipped version on the next upgrade, and
# `systemctl edit heimdall` can override it per-host without touching either file.
#
# A bare level is scoped to heimdall and leaves its dependencies at "warn". Use a
# full directive to aim at one subsystem, e.g.
# RUST_LOG="warn,heimdall::cardano::blockfrost_chain=debug"
#RUST_LOG="debug"
